19120cbb29605d27c52b0bf475d","position":"1787450711665526001-c5df5bf2-5a51-4ece-b417-f766171a9182"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"0f3009bb35f192ea6f2ad15d7eacfa14ce84c9bcf9c39b776c3797bed6360011","event_uuid":"9d59d276-5a28-470d-99b6-aba418a5ed0a","position":{"commit_sha":"81b21eb4712e843e97ebce8e13c17bfa0c20db5e","position":"1787450812711983001-9d59d276-5a28-470d-99b6-aba418a5ed0a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator decision (2026-08-19): APPROVED — THREAD the captured values through; do not drop the capture.\n\nThread comment_max_chars and jira_cli_timeout from ReconcilerSettings into the built backend and the DC sanitizer, so the DC comment sanitizer stops calling resolve_comment_max_chars() ambiently and uses the compose-captured value instead.\n\nRationale: the two options cost about the same to implement, so cost is not the tiebreaker. Dropping the capture would preserve an ambient global read and revert a deliberate design direction — operation-scoped configuration — that the RP work is actively moving toward. Threading completes that design for these two fields; dropping it re-opens a seam that was intentionally closed.","timestamp":1787173861883127001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation pushed as Gerrit change 2138 (Change-Id I061cd0e61268d8c509c1a6c8c2c748c5595678e3), commit a99498137eb. RED-first tests added then implementation: DC scope->_DCSanitizer(comment_max_chars) threading; _run_acli call_timeout with _effective_call_timeout ambient fallback; call_timeout threaded through the whole acli_cli_ops create/read/comment chain, module-level update_issue, and AcliClient's bypass delegations (create/update/get/comment/delete); _build_cloud passes captured jira_cli_timeout. Verified locally: 3158 reconciler unit tests pass, bridge field-coverage + held-out bindings suites pass (50), make lint PASS, mypy 638 files clean, complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0. Awaiting LLM-Review/Verified on change 2138.","timestamp":1787448373835996001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"MERGED: Gerrit change 2138 merged to main as 30663cb2feef50db21ee5a4375fe590a7075f56b (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1 via CI run 32610311106, 0 unresolved comments; 1 advisory non-blocking finding on --from-json priority create path tests). All 6 acceptance criteria met and ticked: DC scope-threaded sanitizer ceiling (ambient resolve bypassed when scope present, legacy lazy resolve preserved without scope), _run_acli call_timeout bound/fallback semantics, all five AcliClient bypass delegations forward call_timeout, _build_cloud threads captured jira_cli_timeout. Evidence: 3158 reconciler unit tests pass, bridge suites 50 pass, make lint PASS, mypy 638 files clean, complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0 stale=6. Closing.","timestamp":1787450812711983001}],"created_at":1787024834647530001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9e98bc42-f517-4c00-aed8-ea8478ff8eea","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"e042-4780-6c63-4b09"},{"link_uuid":"9e496420-0839-4c5b-976c-96e0b8a02b03","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4cee-8734-7816-4e4c"}],"description":"S2 (e042) ReconcilerSettings captures `comment_max_chars` and `jira_cli_timeout` at compose, but neither is threaded into the built backend: the DC sanitizer's `comment_max_chars()` still calls `resolve_comment_max_chars()` ambiently on first use, and EVERY Cloud ACLI subprocess call still resolves `reconciler.jira_cli_timeout` ambiently inside `_run_acli` (`_acli_call_timeout()`). Complete the operation-scoped capture for these two fields. Advisory finding from Gerrit 1843 PS1 LLM-Review.\n\n## Approach\n\n**DC `comment_max_chars`:**\n- `JiraDataCenterBackend.__init__` (src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py): when a captured `scope` is present, construct `self.sanitizer = _DCSanitizer(comment_max_chars=scope.comment_max_chars)` via the existing injection seam; `scope is None` keeps the legacy lazy ambient resolve. `<= 0` already means UNLIMITED in `_truncate_dc_comment_body`, matching `resolve_dc_comment_max_chars`'s 0 convention, so the captured value threads verbatim.\n\n**Cloud `jira_cli_timeout` — thread through EVERY ACLI subprocess chokepoint, not just `AcliClient._run`.** The enumerated `_run_acli` call sites that bypass `_run` (each already threads `acli_cmd` the same way; `call_timeout` rides alongside it):\n- `acli_subprocess._run_acli` (src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py) gains `call_timeout: int | None = None`; a positive value bounds `communicate(timeout=...)`, non-positive/`None` falls back to the existing ambient `_acli_call_timeout()` via a tiny `_effective_call_timeout` helper (keeps `_run_acli`'s McCabe score flat), so direct/legacy constructions stay byte-identical.\n- `acli_cli_ops` (src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_cli_ops.py): `call_timeout: int | None = None` added and forwarded through the whole create/read/comment call chain that spawns ACLI — `_create_issue_no_json` (direct `_run_acli`), `_create_from_json_payload` (direct), `_create_issue_from_json`, `create_issue`, `_verify_created_issue`, `get_issue` (direct), `add_comment` (direct), `get_comments` (direct).\n- `acli.py` module-level `update_issue` gains `call_timeout: int | None = None` forwarded to its direct `_run_acli` WRITE.\n- `AcliClient.__init__` gains keyword `call_timeout: int = 0`, stored as `self._call_timeout`; `_run` forwards it to `_run_acli`, and every delegation that bypasses `_run` passes it explicitly: `create_issue` -> `acli_cli_ops.create_issue`, `update_issue` -> module `update_issue`, `get_issue` -> `acli_cli_ops.get_issue`, `add_comment` -> `acli_cli_ops.add_comment`, and `delete_issue`'s direct `_run_acli`. (`AcliClient.get_comments` and the graph mixin already route through `self._run`.)\n- `ReconcilerRuntime._build_cloud` (src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/runtime.py): pass `call_timeout=s.jira_cli_timeout` when building the real `AcliClient`.\n\n**Explicit scope-outs (stated, intentional):** `update_priority`, `transition_issue`, `unassign_issue` and the `_rest_urlopen_with_retry`/direct-REST paths spawn no ACLI subprocess — their fixed urlopen timeouts are not `jira_cli_timeout` and are unchanged. Legacy module-level entry points invoked without a `call_timeout` (no composed runtime) keep the ambient `_acli_call_timeout()` resolve — that is the compatibility floor, not a gap in the operation-scoped capture.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A DC backend built with a captured scope truncates comments at the scope's `comment_max_chars` without consulting ambient config — RED-first test monkeypatches `resolve_comment_max_chars` to return a different value and asserts the scope value wins; verified by `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_operation_bindings_runtime.py -q`.\n- [x] A DC backend built WITHOUT a scope keeps the legacy lazy ambient resolve — existing bug-049e coverage stays green; verified by `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler -k \"dc or datacenter\" -q`.\n- [x] `_run_acli(call_timeout=N)` bounds the subprocess wait at N seconds while unset/0/None falls back to `_acli_call_timeout()` — pinned by unit tests; verified by `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_acli_subprocess_timeout.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_operation_bindings_runtime.py -q`.\n- [x] Every enumerated bypass site forwards the captured timeout: an `AcliClient(call_timeout=N)` create/update/get/comment/delete call reaches `_run_acli` with `call_timeout=N` (no ambient resolve) — asserted by a RED-first test monkeypatching `acli_subprocess._run_acli` and recording the kwarg across all five client methods; verified by `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_operation_bindings_runtime.py -q`.\n- [x] `ReconcilerRuntime._build_cloud` threads the captured `jira_cli_timeout` into the constructed `AcliClient` — asserted in the runtime bindings test; verified by `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_operation_bindings_runtime.py -q`.\n- [x] Gates pass: `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` (new=0 increased=0) all exit 0.\n\n## Testing\n\nRED-first: add failing tests in `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_operation_bindings_runtime.py` (scope-threaded DC sanitizer ceiling; `AcliClient` `call_timeout` forwarding across `create_issue`/`update_issue`/`get_issue`/`add_comment`/`delete_issue` via a recording `_run_acli` monkeypatch; `_build_cloud` wiring), confirm they fail, then implement until green. `_run_acli`'s own bound/fallback behaviour is tested where its timeout tests live (`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_acli_subprocess_timeout.py`). Regression: `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler -q`, plus `make lint` and `make typecheck`.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py","reason":"thread captured scope comment_max_chars into _DCSanitizer"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py","reason":"AcliClient call_timeout stored and forwarded through _run and every bypass delegation (create/update/get/comment/delete)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_cli_ops.py","reason":"call_timeout threaded through create/read/comment chain to direct _run_acli sites"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py","reason":"_run_acli call_timeout parameter with _effective_call_timeout ambient fallback"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/runtime.py","reason":"_build_cloud passes captured jira_cli_timeout"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_operation_bindings_runtime.py","reason":"RED-first tests for the threaded capture"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_acli_subprocess_timeout.py","reason":"_run_acli explicit call_timeout bound/fallback tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","4cee-8734-7816-4e4c"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"f792ba0d-aafc-4901-85fd-766fc4fbcd98","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2048-d289-e55f-4595","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-04 follow-up: thread captured comment_max_chars/jira_cli_timeout into the built reconciler backend/sanitizer","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c609b1ed-3fc4-4903-b764-350bcb6a9a1a","9e496420-0839-4c5b-976c-96e0b8a02b03","19b2ece5-b6e2-42cc-9aeb-ff515b9ce6df","18e33992-8e5a-4e87-8637-c36d54455dc9","4cb9ee36-1cce-41f2-978c-193231a03d06","d84a18b8-1be7-4758-963a-bea01b7a55b5","8c81cb6a-84a1-4994-a162-cdb5ba60330e","f792ba0d-aafc-4901-85fd-766fc4fbcd98","a69b8d4d-67c2-49f7-946b-8f0d75e48c8a","f5251fb5-631c-444d-9e91-76a8cce0de7b","c5df5bf2-5a51-4ece-b417-f766171a9182","9d59d276-5a28-470d-99b6-aba418a5ed0a"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787450812711983002,"uuid":"e6f432d0-8e50-4a9c-b5c8-de061055506e"}